pancake is one library you can hold several ways. Every surface puts the same
CapTP conversation on the wire, so choose the one that matches how you work.

[One core under every surface, so the one you hold never changes what a session puts on the wire.]($image.siteAsset('diagram-surfaces.svg'))

| Surface | You write | Reach for it when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Zig package]($link.page('start')) | Zig | you want the full engine and types |
| [C ABI](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md) | C / any FFI | embedding, or wrapping a language with no binding yet |
| [Bindings]($link.page('bindings')) | Rust, TypeScript, Python, Racket | you are already in one of those four |
| [CapTP CLI]($link.page('cli')) | shell / MCP | call, host, REPL, or agent MCP (`zig build`, then `zig-out/bin/pancake`) |

The bindings surface reaches one more place: the TypeScript binding compiles to
WebAssembly, so a session runs in the browser too ([Bindings]($link.page('bindings'))).

Each surface has its own front door. [Start building]($link.page('start'))
walks the Zig round-trip line by line, and the
[Zig API]($link.page('reference/api')) lists every declaration. The C archives
ship generated headers, inventoried in the
[API reference]($link.page('reference')), and
[consuming-from-c](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md)
walks a first C program. [Bindings]($link.page('bindings')) carries each
language's idiom. The [CapTP CLI]($link.page('cli')) page shows the shell happy
path, and
[docs/cli.md](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/cli.md)
has more recipes.

## One engine

A Zig peer, a C consumer, and any binding hold the same OCapN conversation byte
for byte. The codec and CapTP version come from negotiation against the
partner's offers, not from the surface you built on
([Concepts]($link.page('concepts'))). Every artifact comes from `zig build`, and
`zig build check` runs the in-tree verification. The
[README](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/README.md#build)
lists the common steps. The `tcp` wire is cleartext, and encrypted channels come
from the iroh and WebRTC transports ([Transports]($link.page('transports'))).
